WEBVTT

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:18.330
Don't underestimate grown-ups.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:20.790
And don't you underestimate grade-schoolers.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:57.180
We met our goal
for the first week of August!

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.140
August Visitors

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.140
Goal

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.140
We've gotten a lot more visitors!

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:05.310
The touch pools and shaved ice were a hit.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.820
Although the shaved ice lost money.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:10.080
We got a lot of followers on Penstagram, too.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:11.470
Well, Gramps?

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:14.180
What do you think of my work
as Acting Director?

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.000
And I'm sure if we keep it up,

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.200
there won't be any more talk
about the aquarium shutting down.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:27.050
Summer break is the busy season.

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:29.760
Let's work hard for the
next month! No breaks!

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:30.880
Hang on.

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:36.890
Do you have any idea how many shifts
I've had without any breaks?

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:40.080
I had to fill in for Umi-yan while he was sick
and for the director while he was out of town.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:42.060
I never took any breaks,
even when I got more work.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:44.860
I feel bad about that.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:47.050
But it's make-or-break time.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:48.620
If we all work hard together—

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:50.820
S-S-S-Stop.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:59.790
Giving your staff time to rest is
an important part of your job as director.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:02.660
It's been a while since you've
taken a break, too, Kukuru.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.000
I don't need a break.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.520
Umi-yan's back, too.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.910
Why don't you young ones
take some time off together?

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:13.880
We can manage for a day.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:16.050
We'll take care of it!

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.480
Nice, nice!

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.080
It's summer break.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:25.300
Let's hang out together!

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:28.140
I want to work!

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:31.000
Your Gramps has a point.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.920
I have a lot of paid vacation days saved up.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:34.520
I have to take a break, too.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:37.280
Let's go somewhere
you want to go, Fuuka-chan.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.000
Tell us where you want to go.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.730
I...

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.090
I want to go to the beach.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.660
That's so ordinary.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:48.240
How about a classic barbecue, then?

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:50.750
Let's invite Kai-kun
and Yakamashi Kuuya, too.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:53.920
As a reward from Director Kukuru.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.800
"To Yakamashi Kuuya,"

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:58.670
Must Read!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:58.670
To Yakamashi Kuuya

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:59.980
"Come to our barbecue. Free booze."

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:00.880
Why his full name?

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:03.340
"Your beloved Kai-kun will be there."

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:03.340
They were classmates
and frenemies, apparently.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.120
Oh, I heard about that.

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.420
Work!

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:19.940
Komaka Island

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:21.270
I haven't gone swimming in forever.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:24.660
When are you coming out of hiding?

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.060
This isn't like you.

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:27.530
Just accept it.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:29.360
All right.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:31.030
I'm going to have fun for the day!

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:36.650
Huh?

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:38.780
Hey, that's a cute swimsuit.

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:40.090
It's so Tokyo-ish.

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:42.120
Where are your swimsuits?

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.220
People here don't wear them much.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:45.900
Especially because the UV rays are so harsh.

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:50.700
I had it sent from home in a hurry,
because we were going to the beach.

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:53.610
And this is from one of my photo shoots.

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:55.310
I'm going to get changed!

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:56.680
Don't worry about it.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:57.190
See?

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:00.690
The tourists are all in swimsuits.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:01.930
But...

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:03.780
Who cares? Let's go!

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:54.440
Wow, there are so many!

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:56.520
All the same fish that are at Gama Gama.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:00.730
Isn't it awesome how you can get
even more up-close to them at the beach?

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:01.550
Yeah!

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:07.560
Gramps always says that the aquarium
is the first step to learning about sea life.

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:11.580
He wants people to take interest
in the world of real sea life, too.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.560
You're talking about work again.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:17.310
That's what crappy bosses do.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:18.490
Fine.

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:20.840
That was fun.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.560
It was beautiful here.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:24.360
You must be getting hungry.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:28.860
Kai-kun and the others came early
to set up the barbecue for us.

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:30.010
And...

00:06:30.010 --> 00:06:31.740
Does it have to be...

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:32.870
Here?

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.410
We're right in front of Gama Gama.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.350
We're so close.

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:39.750
Too close.

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.630
Come on. It's all right.

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:42.650
It was last minute.

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:44.970
We're lucky we found a spot at all.

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:46.520
There they are.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:52.050
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:53.480
Hello.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:55.880
We just started cooking the meat.

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:57.020
Good timing.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:58.390
Thanks!

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:00.390
Huh?

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:03.650
Thank you for inviting me today.

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:06.040
She came.

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:07.650
She had to come.

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:08.730
Sorry.

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:10.350
I tried to stop her, but it didn't work.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:12.220
I can picture it happening.

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:14.030
This is my sister.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:15.550
Nice to meet you.

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:17.440
I'm his sister, Maho.

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:19.580
My brother's been in your care.

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:21.440
Nice to meet you.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:22.670
Fuuka-chan, right?

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.590
I've heard about you from my brother!

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:27.210
Wow, he's right.

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:28.510
You're so cute!

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:30.200
Maho, keep it down.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.470
You're disturbing the neighbors.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.040
Please, Kukuru, stay out of my way.

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:36.620
I'm talking to Fuuka-chan right now.

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:38.730
Here we go.

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:40.390
They never get along.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.940
You smell nice, Fuuka-chan.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.810
Kukuru smells like fish.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:46.950
You're nothing like her.

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:49.580
What's wrong with smelling fishy?

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:51.320
You're a fisherman's daughter.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:53.520
Fuuka-chan's not as rural.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:55.130
She smells like Tokyo.

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:57.770
Fuuka's from Iwate.

00:07:58.470 --> 00:07:59.740
Onii-chan!

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:02.110
If you're going to date anyone,
it should be Fuuka-chan.

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:03.480
Don't ever date Kukuru!

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:05.420
What are you talking about?!

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:08.630
I want a sister that's like Fuuka-chan.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:11.130
Marry Fuuka-chan, please, Onii-chan.

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:12.380
Please?

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:15.200
Damn this brat!

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:17.920
I really can't handle elementary-school girls.

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:26.690
Seems like Maho-chan really likes Fuuka-chan.

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:27.500
Yeah.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:29.130
She's pretty.

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:31.190
I can see why a kid would admire her.

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:34.120
I've wanted an older sister before, too.

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:36.120
I know how she feels.

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:39.520
You're an only child, aren't you, Udon-chan?

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:40.840
I am.

00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:43.370
My parents work me so hard.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:45.080
Haven't you ever felt like that?

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:47.680
Have you wanted siblings?

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:48.860
I have.

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:50.050
For sports festivals and stuff.

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:51.680
Totally.

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:58.490
When families gets together for lunch,
the ones with siblings seem so lively.

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:01.060
They seem to be having so much fun.

00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:04.810
You know how the siblings
who are close go halfsies and stuff?

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:08.790
I've always envied that kind of thing.

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:11.040
I know.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:14.940
You get different toys,
and you get to share clothes.

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:16.280
I was so jealous.

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:17.360
Exactly.

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:18.700
I bought ice cream.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:19.850
Yay!

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:21.080
Thanks, Fuuka.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:24.080
Eat it before it melts.

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:26.120
You bought so many kinds.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:27.600
Thank you!

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.080
Which one should I have?

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:31.230
This one looks good, too.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:32.590
I can't decide.

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.670
Want to go halfsies, then?

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:38.460
Okay.

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:43.080
Here.

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:45.640
I'll go hand out the rest.

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:48.770
Fuuka-chan's kind of like
your older sister, huh?

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:51.230
Yeah.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.160
Which one do you want, Maho?

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:02.540
An older sister, huh?

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:05.110
Shoot, it's melting!

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:11.040
1

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:25.070
I'm just going to take
a quick peek before I go.

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:26.100
Huh?

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:28.810
What are you doing here, Kuuya-kun?

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:29.730
Hi.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:32.240
It's your day off.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:35.020
Aren't you having a barbecue?

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:36.740
It's not really my thing.

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:41.050
You say that, but you're really here
because you're worried about work, aren't you?

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:44.990
Kukuru might come to take a peek
at some point, too.

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:47.250
Is it busy inside?

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:49.670
We're just fine.

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:53.560
You didn't have to give everyone
the same day off.

00:10:53.560 --> 00:11:01.260
I need to get you and Kukuru
used to life without Gama Gama.

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:05.820
You wouldn't be ready for it if it were
to go away right at the end of August.

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:08.120
You'll burn out.

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:12.170
You haven't contacted Tingaara yet?

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:13.770
I'm sorry.

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:18.980
Their director was worried
that you might not come.

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:23.210
I didn't feel like doing it
until we were done here.

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:25.660
What are they talking about?

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:29.450
At least say "hi" to them, would you?

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:33.670
How can you be so calm, Director?

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:38.040
I seriously don't even care
about finding a new job.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:39.820
I just...

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:47.060
I'd be grateful if you
continued working here.

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:50.980
Take your time to decide.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:10.150
Kukuru.

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:15.510
Fuuka.

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:23.470
What's wrong?

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:26.140
You just vanished all of a sudden.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:31.640
I don't know if I'm going to be okay.

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:34.730
Are we going to make it?

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:37.650
I don't really have time to waste.

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:43.540
Gramps is getting ready
to close the aquarium.

00:12:44.420 --> 00:12:45.940
If we don't do something...

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:53.410
You aren't alone.

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:56.290
I'll be right here with you, Kukuru.

00:12:59.990 --> 00:13:00.800
Thanks.

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:07.560
I'm talking about work again.

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:09.690
That thing "crappy bosses" do?

00:13:09.690 --> 00:13:10.680
Yeah.

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:15.160
Onii-chan, let me introduce you.

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:16.680
This is my friend.

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:18.540
I just met him over there.

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:21.690
I'm Chinen Rui.
I'm in Maho-chan's class.

00:13:22.550 --> 00:13:24.560
I'm in the running
to be Maho-chan's boyfriend.

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:26.820
Pleased to meet you, Onii-san.

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:28.090
"Onii-san"?!

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:29.950
Oh, stop it, Rui-Rui.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:34.330
I plan on dating only
the person I'm going to marry.

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:37.710
It has to be someone good-looking,
like my brother.

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:39.480
Like your brother, huh?

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:40.750
Good-looking?

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:44.460
Please don't take
what she's saying seriously.

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:48.430
I feel like I've seen Rui-kun somewhere.

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:50.970
He's a regular at Gama Gama Aquarium.

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:52.930
I have an annual pass!

00:13:54.260 --> 00:13:57.200
Rui-kun's a fish professor. Right?

00:13:57.200 --> 00:13:58.940
He knows so much.

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:00.840
Wow, that's so awesome.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:02.520
More than your brother.

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:04.400
Shut up, Udon-chan.

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:06.610
Yakamashi-san.

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:09.500
Hey! Why is he here?

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:10.870
I'm surprised, too.

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:13.440
No wonder you weren't at the aquarium.

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:15.370
You're messing around here.

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:18.750
That must be why it's closing down.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:20.750
Do those two not get along?

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:24.010
Rui-kun thinks Kuuya-san is his rival.

00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:27.880
He's always showing off
his fish knowledge.

00:14:28.420 --> 00:14:31.300
Question: Where do spotnape
cardinalfish lay their eggs?

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:32.850
Inside the male's mouth.

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:36.600
Next question: How does the
bluestreak cleaner wrasse sleep?

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:39.690
It makes a mucus sleeping bag
and sleeps in the cracks between rocks.

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:46.070
I told you not to bother
competing against me.

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:51.150
So Kukuru fights with Maho-chan,
and Yakamashi fights with Rui-kun?

00:14:51.150 --> 00:14:53.900
They're grade schoolers.
What are you both doing?

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:56.170
Maybe you two are quite alike.

00:14:56.170 --> 00:14:57.760
You and Kuuya-san.

00:14:57.760 --> 00:14:58.910
No we aren't!

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:00.790
I don't hate girls!

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:03.020
Listen up, Yakamashi.

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:03.790
What?

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:06.560
Rui-kun has a crush on Maho-chan.

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:07.950
He wants to impress her.

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:08.550
Get it?

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:09.400
What?

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:12.050
Just cut him some slack!

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:13.800
Be a grown-up!

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:16.310
What else are you good at, Rui-kun?

00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:18.810
Running.

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:21.480
Why don't you try running a race
against him, then?

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:22.540
Sure.

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:25.770
Yakamashi-san doesn't seem very fit, though.

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:26.860
Is he going to be all right?

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:27.560
What?

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:29.490
Ow!

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:33.240
You might be able to beat him
in beach flags, then.

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:35.080
Right, Rui-kun?

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:35.990
Yes.

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:37.080
Right?

00:15:38.690 --> 00:15:41.000
What a pain in the ass.

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:55.220
Don't underestimate grown-ups.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:57.680
And don't you underestimate grade-schoolers.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:08.510
Crap, he's got serious eyes.

00:16:08.510 --> 00:16:10.730
Is Kuuya-san a sore loser?

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:13.910
Hey, you better go easy on him!

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:15.160
It's fine.

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:16.810
I'll be all right.

00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:20.000
I really want to impress her.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:21.470
Is he really in elementary school?

00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:22.870
What is this, a shoujo manga?

00:16:24.280 --> 00:16:28.380
Please go on a date with me
if I win this race, Maho-chan!

00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:30.760
I'll think about it.

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:34.510
All right, I have to win!

00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:39.310
You don't know what
you've got coming, do you?

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:41.720
What are you talking about?

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:44.760
You should experience defeat early on.

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:48.310
On your mark...

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:50.820
Get set...

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:52.990
Go!

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:00.160
Go...

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:16.260
It's mine!

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:23.080
Ow!

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:24.880
What are you doing
taking it so seriously? Idiot.

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:27.260
You're such a child, Kuuya-san.

00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:29.230
Shut up, girls.

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:40.680
Rui-Rui, you lost, but you looked
kind of awesome when you were running.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:42.870
Maho-chan...

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:45.260
I'll win for sure next time.

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:48.370
Watch me beat Yakamashi-san.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:50.380
Good luck.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:51.190
Yeah!

00:17:51.190 --> 00:17:53.690
Grade-schoolers sure are simple.

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:56.350
Having Maho around throws me off.

00:17:56.350 --> 00:17:59.360
Is that why you're working all summer?

00:18:00.250 --> 00:18:01.350
No.

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:04.350
That's not really it.

00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:10.520
Yum!

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:11.450
Lucky.

00:18:11.450 --> 00:18:12.900
Booze.

00:18:13.410 --> 00:18:15.650
Hurry and grow up.

00:18:16.230 --> 00:18:18.380
Where did Maho-chan and Rui-kun go?

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:20.660
They went home before it got dark.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:23.550
Jeez, Yakamashi Kuuya...

00:18:23.550 --> 00:18:26.330
He's such a tight-ass.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:29.670
Karin-san, what is Kuuya-san like?

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:33.500
I can't really figure him out,
even though I've been working with him.

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:37.300
Well...

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:39.720
That was unusual.

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.580
Huh? What was?

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:46.510
You were running for real
back there, weren't you?

00:18:46.510 --> 00:18:48.600
You always seem so indifferent.

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:49.840
Not at all!

00:18:49.840 --> 00:18:52.970
I was only giving it, like, twenty percent.

00:18:53.700 --> 00:18:56.190
You're a different person
when you're drunk, aren't you?

00:18:56.510 --> 00:18:58.070
Sure, whatever.

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:04.440
Sometimes, after you've grown up,
you have an urge to drink.

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:07.440
You know, Kai-kun...

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:08.970
What is it?

00:19:08.970 --> 00:19:12.040
Did you know I quit high school?

00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:14.120
Uh, no...

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:17.300
Believe it or not,
I've been through a lot.

00:19:17.890 --> 00:19:20.720
He was in my class in high school.

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:23.420
He was pretty popular, too.

00:19:23.420 --> 00:19:25.900
He had good grades, and he was athletic.

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:27.680
And he's pretty good-looking.

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:34.650
He got asked out by a girl
who was the center of a mean-girl clique.

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:41.450
He turned her down because he wasn't interested,
and the group came after him.

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:45.320
They started spreading crazy rumors.

00:19:45.320 --> 00:19:47.980
It got out of hand,
and the police got involved.

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:50.460
The school started treating him
like a problem child, too.

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:54.000
He became disillusioned with girls
and the grown-ups around him.

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:58.840
And he stopped talking,
and eventually, he quit school.

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:00.520
Seriously?

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:06.920
I quit school on a whim, but it wasn't like
there was anything I wanted to do.

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:11.120
I was lost for a while,
until Kukuru's gramps took me in.

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:12.600
Kuuya-kun!

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.600
Take these for me, please.

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:16.680
Yes, sir...

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:19.720
Kuuya-kun!

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:21.110
Could you do these, please?

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:22.860
Yes, sir....

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:25.310
Kuuya-kun!

00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:26.820
Yes, sir!

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:28.760
He was working me to death.

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:33.210
I got pissed, and I figured
I'd try testing the director.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:36.210
Encyclopedia of World Aquatic Life

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:40.190
Director, if you can't answer these questions,
you have to let me do less work.

00:20:40.190 --> 00:20:41.370
Sure.

00:20:41.370 --> 00:20:43.090
Ask me anything.

00:20:43.520 --> 00:20:46.010
<i>Alveopora japonica</i> have twelve tentacles.

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:47.600
How many do <i>Goniopora lobata</i> have?

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:49.100
Twenty-four.

00:20:50.820 --> 00:20:52.010
Correct.

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:57.450
He answers everything.

00:20:57.450 --> 00:21:03.320
I thought he was just some slow old fogey,
but he might be a genius.

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:07.320
I ended up getting hooked on it.

00:21:09.990 --> 00:21:14.700
There are all kinds of unique
creatures in the aquarium.

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:17.550
The staff can be, too.

00:21:17.550 --> 00:21:20.820
As long as they do their work.

00:21:22.310 --> 00:21:25.530
He taught me all kinds of things.

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:29.010
It was way more fun than school.

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:32.120
Closing is...

00:21:34.360 --> 00:21:35.270
bullshit!

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:43.230
Kai.

00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:45.520
We're heading home.

00:21:45.520 --> 00:21:47.280
Okay, got it.

00:21:50.530 --> 00:21:52.300
I'm worried, too.

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:54.630
About her.

00:21:58.530 --> 00:22:02.470
I don't know if she can handle
Gama Gama closing.
